Sure! To sort your `myItemList` so that all items with a status of `'urgent'` appear first, followed by the rest sorted alphabetically by name in ascending order, you can use the following function:

```json
{
  "function": "prioritizeAndSort",
  "arguments": {
    "items": "[{\"name\": \"Task A\", \"status\": \"normal\"}, {\"name\": \"Task B\", \"status\": \"urgent\"}]",
    "priorityStatus": "\"urgent\"",
    "ascending": "true"
  }
}
```

Replace the example array inside `"items"` with your actual `myItemList`. Once you run this, you'll get the sorted result. If you'd like me to apply it to your real list, just paste the full array here and I'll execute the function for you.
